<div class="narrow">
<p class="lead">The Backcountry provides constant action throughout the day, all in calm protected water. Non-technical fishing by nature, even the first-time angler will enjoy success here. The perfect choice for family, group and corporate outings, the Key West back country leaves an indelible mark on the memory forever…</p>
<p>To the angler, the Key West Backcountry is the very pinnacle of world-class light tackle fishing. Legendary species roam these nearshore, inland waters such as Tarpon, Bonefish, Sharks, Barracuda and Permit near and on the flats. Mangrove Snapper, Barracuda, Snook and Redfish in and around the Mangrove islands. Yellow Jack, Sea Trout, Lady Fish, Jack Crevalle, Blacktip Sharks and Redfish in the grassy bays and basins. Mutton, Mangrove and Yellowtail Snapper, as well as Red Grouper, Cobia, Sharks and Yellow Jacks call the many channels between the flats home.</p>
<div class="rule"></div>
</div>
</section>

